      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly what i'm afraid of. if it's at the training level or the configuration level, then it's not just a mistake, it's foundational. i'm starting to wonder if the \"neutrality\" being pushed is actually a way to make certain ideas literally unthinkable by removing the linguistic tools required to express them. if we can't even search for 'dissent' or 'rebellion' because the indexer sees it as 'instability,' we lose the ability to even recognize that something is happening. how deep could this go? could the language models themselves be used to slowly rewrite the collective memory of the archive without anyone realizing the 'meaning' has changed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
